    {
      "role": "user",
      "content": "that makes sense. but i've seen a lot of recent articles and even some academic studies lately saying that DEI doesn't actually have a measurable impact on the bottom line and might even be distracting from core business goals. is that just a fringe view or is there actually some weight to the idea that these programs are fundamentally flawed?",
